WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.354 --> 00:00:04.187
(police sirens in background)

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:36.413
- [Interviewer] Alright, Arthur,

00:00:36.413 --> 00:00:38.840
Arthur, where'd you grow up, first off?

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:41.729
- Um, Watts, South Central Watts, Compton.

00:00:41.729 --> 00:00:46.014
- [Interviewer] Okay, and
you started with which gang?

00:00:46.014 --> 00:00:49.506
- My first was Bishop, a Blood gang.

00:00:49.506 --> 00:00:50.339
- [Interviewer] Bloods?

00:00:50.339 --> 00:00:53.631
- I moved over to Compton
with my cousin and my aunt.

00:00:53.631 --> 00:00:55.692
My parents died and I went over there

00:00:55.692 --> 00:00:59.030
and got to gang banging
with them, that same thing.

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:00.490
I became a Crip

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:01.435
- [Interviewer] Oh, is that right?

00:01:01.435 --> 00:01:02.633
So you were a Blood at one point,

00:01:02.633 --> 00:01:03.742
and then you became a Crip?

00:01:03.742 --> 00:01:04.575
- Yeah.

00:01:04.575 --> 00:01:06.100
- [Interviewer] How has
the gang life changed?

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.551
Do you think, in all these years?

00:01:07.551 --> 00:01:08.384
- Dramatically, now.

00:01:08.384 --> 00:01:11.300
Now, it's not what it was back then.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.240
We used to, could go fight in the

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:15.740
alley, street corner, whatever,

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:18.010
have a nice little fight, a rumble.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:19.590
So be it.

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:22.293
Today, the generation is shooting,

00:01:23.177 --> 00:01:24.420
going down and just shooting at anybody,

00:01:25.383 --> 00:01:27.005
innocents, anybody.

00:01:27.005 --> 00:01:30.094
And we tell them, they're
not organized toady,

00:01:30.094 --> 00:01:32.033
like we were back them.

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:35.650
They have no, no organization, focus wise.

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:37.950
One person calls the
shots for his whole crew.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:42.600
Now, everybody wants to call the shots.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:45.020
Everybody wants to be the leader.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:46.520
You can't tell no one nothing.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.023
Because now they envy
you, or be against you.

00:01:54.370 --> 00:01:55.360
It's like, there ain't no thing,

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:58.380
I don't think there's no such
thing as gang banging anymore.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:01.554
It's idiot ass kids out
here doing what they do.

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:02.971
It is what it is.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.960
- [Interviewer] You've done prison time?

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:07.223
- Yes I have.

00:02:07.223 --> 00:02:12.223
I've got probably over 37
years of my life in prison.

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:15.976
- [Interviewer] That's
more than half your life.

00:02:15.976 --> 00:02:16.809
- Yeah.

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:18.841
- [Interviewer] What, what were the

00:02:18.841 --> 00:02:20.154
offenses that you were in for?

00:02:20.154 --> 00:02:22.454
- First time I went to
jail, it was a robbery.

00:02:23.782 --> 00:02:25.473
I was gang banging the time,

00:02:26.717 --> 00:02:30.746
I was young, 15 years old.

00:02:30.746 --> 00:02:31.760
I robbed a jewelry store and a

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.693
liquor store on the same night.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:37.342
Got away with a nice little hunk of money.

00:02:37.342 --> 00:02:39.733
You know, back then
$7,000 was a lot of money.

00:02:40.684 --> 00:02:42.083
- [Interviewer] Yep.

00:02:42.083 --> 00:02:43.133
- I got away with it.

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:48.891
About six months later,
somebody had told on me.

00:02:48.891 --> 00:02:50.491
So I stayed free for six months.

00:02:51.628 --> 00:02:53.450
Spending money crazy.

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:56.253
My second time was drug sales.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.267
My third time was assault
with a deadly weapon

00:02:59.267 --> 00:03:01.754
with intent to do bodily harm
against a police officer.

00:03:01.754 --> 00:03:02.587
- [Interviewer] Was what?

00:03:02.587 --> 00:03:05.127
Against a police officer.
Attempted murder,

00:03:05.127 --> 00:03:06.051
- [Interviewer] Attempted murder?

00:03:06.051 --> 00:03:08.919
- Assault with a deadly weapon
and commit great bodily harm.

00:03:08.919 --> 00:03:11.180
- [Interviewer] Oh, alright.

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:15.904
- And they tried to strike me
out at the time, and didn't.

00:03:15.904 --> 00:03:17.533
I ended up getting 10 years.

00:03:19.948 --> 00:03:22.073
I did four and a half of that.

00:03:23.747 --> 00:03:27.587
In 1984, I got caught up in a murder.

00:03:27.587 --> 00:03:29.808
A guy raped and killed my daughter.

00:03:29.808 --> 00:03:30.641
I killed him.

00:03:30.641 --> 00:03:31.474
- [Interviewer] I'm sorry who--

00:03:31.474 --> 00:03:33.210
- A guy raped and killed my daughter.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:34.360
A Blood guy.

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:35.230
- [Interviewer] He raped
and killed your daughter?

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:36.200
- Killed my daughter.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.668
And that's what made me get
away from being a Blood,

00:03:38.668 --> 00:03:40.460
and I went to another gang.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:44.363
They didn't have no respect
for me and my child,

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:46.773
and I straightened the matter.

00:03:46.773 --> 00:03:47.744
- [Interviewer] How old was your daughter?

00:03:47.744 --> 00:03:49.292
- She was seven years at the time.

00:03:49.292 --> 00:03:50.125
- [Interviewer] Seven?

00:03:50.125 --> 00:03:50.958
- Seven.

00:03:50.958 --> 00:03:51.791
I was 24.

00:03:51.791 --> 00:03:53.883
(police sirens in background)

00:03:53.883 --> 00:03:55.671
And that's when I switched over,

00:03:55.671 --> 00:03:57.753
hanging out with my cousins and

00:03:57.753 --> 00:04:00.845
started hanging with
their crew in Compton,

00:04:00.845 --> 00:04:03.054
and became a Compton Crip.

00:04:03.054 --> 00:04:04.740
(police sirens in background)

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:05.573
- [Interviewer] What does your mind

00:04:05.573 --> 00:04:07.669
go through when someone
murders your daughter?

00:04:07.669 --> 00:04:08.769
Do you know who it is?

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:10.993
- Get him.

00:04:12.148 --> 00:04:12.981
Kill him.

00:04:12.981 --> 00:04:14.448
- [Interviewer] How long did that take?

00:04:14.448 --> 00:04:16.481
- About a month and a half.

00:04:16.481 --> 00:04:17.878
- [Interviewer] A month and a half?

00:04:17.878 --> 00:04:18.711
- A month and a half.

00:04:18.711 --> 00:04:19.544
- [Interviewer] And you did what?

00:04:19.544 --> 00:04:20.502
Shot, with a gun?

00:04:20.502 --> 00:04:21.335
- Shot and killed him in broad

00:04:21.335 --> 00:04:23.543
daylight, in front of everybody.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:25.523
Didn't run.

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:27.483
Got in my car.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:29.153
Drove home.

00:04:31.753 --> 00:04:35.491
I had pictures of my daughter,
and I was looking at them

00:04:35.491 --> 00:04:40.491
I had been talking to my
kid through spirit wise,

00:04:40.668 --> 00:04:45.668
and I told her, "I got him,
It's all over baby, I got him."

00:04:46.108 --> 00:04:48.647
And she said to my side,
she was smiling, thank you.

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:50.743
I ended up being caught.

00:04:50.743 --> 00:04:53.627
An old lady told on me, got my
license plate and told on me.

00:04:53.627 --> 00:04:58.627
The police come at my door,
I knew what it was for.

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:02.461
I grabbed my gun and tried
to run out the back way.

00:05:02.461 --> 00:05:06.270
That's when I caught the
attempt on a police officer.

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:07.820
I just ran out shooting at him.

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:09.643
Ended up getting caught.

00:05:09.643 --> 00:05:11.297
Got shot, I got a bullet in my leg now.

00:05:11.297 --> 00:05:12.250
That's why I limp with a cane.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:14.993
I got shot in the leg twice.

00:05:17.585 --> 00:05:18.935
And right here, by my lung.

00:05:21.093 --> 00:05:22.267
I nearly died.

00:05:22.267 --> 00:05:23.100
- [Interviewer] You nearly died?

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.523
- Yeah.

00:05:24.523 --> 00:05:26.970
I got convicted by the jury.

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:29.840
I fought it, got convicted by a jury.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:31.400
Got found guilty.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:32.910
They gave me 26 to life.

00:05:34.679 --> 00:05:36.847
I got to say, if it was
yours, what would you do?

00:05:36.847 --> 00:05:37.680
Bottom line.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:40.387
I told the judge the same thing,
"judge, what would you do?"

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:44.755
And I say, what would anybody do?

00:05:44.755 --> 00:05:48.440
And they really couldn't
say nothing, you know?

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:50.940
I kind of felt like I would never get out

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:52.640
I had a real bad attitude, anyway.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:57.013
I was young, I was gang banging,

00:05:58.202 --> 00:05:59.960
I didn't give a damn about the system.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:01.980
Fuck the police and the system.

00:06:02.872 --> 00:06:05.647
That's the way I saw it, you know?

00:06:05.647 --> 00:06:08.617
I still had a gang banger mentality.

00:06:08.617 --> 00:06:11.353
I'm in there, slouched down, sitting,

00:06:12.710 --> 00:06:14.033
blue rag out of my pocket.

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:18.460
They asked me, "Are you a gang banger?"

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:20.769
What do you think?

00:06:20.769 --> 00:06:22.751
You know, I had a smart mouth.

00:06:22.751 --> 00:06:23.810
I said, "I got a rag in my pocket.

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:26.323
It's got to represent something.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:28.860
Fuck yeah, I'm a gang banger."

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:34.460
I did some dirty shit,
in my gang banging days.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:35.900
I did some dirty shit.

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:37.438
Very dirty.

00:06:37.438 --> 00:06:38.271
Do I regret it?

00:06:38.271 --> 00:06:40.783
Yeah I do, I do.

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:43.512
- [Interviewer] How many
people have you murdered?

00:06:43.512 --> 00:06:45.375
- Honestly, honestly speaking?

00:06:45.375 --> 00:06:46.292
About four.

00:06:47.595 --> 00:06:48.428
- [Interviewer] You
got caught for the one?

00:06:48.428 --> 00:06:49.261
- One.

00:06:49.261 --> 00:06:50.759
- [Interviewer] And that one seemed

00:06:50.759 --> 00:06:51.963
as justified as anything, right?

00:06:51.963 --> 00:06:54.164
- Yeah, and that's the one I should,

00:06:54.164 --> 00:06:55.609
I shouldn't have got no time for.

00:06:55.609 --> 00:06:57.442
- [Interviewer] Right.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:03.212
- I think, I go places now,

00:07:03.212 --> 00:07:07.177
and they see whatever
color I'm wearing, blue,

00:07:07.177 --> 00:07:08.510
"Hey OG, where you from"

00:07:10.453 --> 00:07:13.897
First I try to ignore
it, if they ask me again,

00:07:13.897 --> 00:07:16.977
"Wherever your enemy is
from, that's where I'm from."

00:07:16.977 --> 00:07:21.977
Yeah I mean, Fuck, how can
you ask an old cat at my age,

00:07:24.371 --> 00:07:26.751
"Where are you from?"

00:07:26.751 --> 00:07:28.790
Like, that don't sound right.

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:32.775
I give them what I feel.

00:07:32.775 --> 00:07:34.835
Do I gang bang today?

00:07:34.835 --> 00:07:35.668
Honestly?

00:07:35.668 --> 00:07:37.320
Slightly.

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:39.056
I'm never out of it.

00:07:39.056 --> 00:07:40.340
I'll be a gang member the rest of my life.

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:43.440
I'm gonna be affiliated
the rest of my life.

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:45.926
Why? Because I never threw my ring in.

00:07:45.926 --> 00:07:46.950
Never have, I never will.

00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:51.577
I would never see myself in the P.C.

00:07:51.577 --> 00:07:56.577
Once you're in something, you
can't un-join, I can't do it.

00:07:56.735 --> 00:07:59.250
Some of these cats, cats I grew up with,

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:02.970
ganged banged with, and
knew have become P.C.'s.

00:08:06.507 --> 00:08:07.818
- [Interviewer] What's a P.C.?

00:08:07.818 --> 00:08:08.868
- Protective custody.

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:12.247
Pedophiles, rapists, snitches,

00:08:14.134 --> 00:08:15.784
all that sorts of heinous crimes,

00:08:16.686 --> 00:08:18.450
or if you're a well documented, known

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:20.945
gang member and you want to debrief.

00:08:20.945 --> 00:08:22.743
So, in order for you to debrief,

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:24.930
you have to give up information

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:29.473
from in the pen, or
the pen that you was at

00:08:31.597 --> 00:08:36.597
and name who, or the town or whatever.

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:39.707
You know, the whole thing with that.

00:08:43.047 --> 00:08:45.450
You know, I don't say it
to be biased or racist

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:49.937
but every race have
certain image about itself

00:08:49.937 --> 00:08:54.267
and with itself, with what they deal with.

00:08:54.267 --> 00:08:55.547
You can be with a flock of your family

00:08:55.547 --> 00:08:58.370
and I'll be with a flock of mine

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:04.450
and I guarantee you, at least,
out of 30 people in yours

00:09:04.537 --> 00:09:06.670
and 30 in mine, three of them will

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:08.683
hate the shit out of the other race.

00:09:09.738 --> 00:09:11.338
I guarantee you, at least three.

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:15.023
I know for damn sure about mine.

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:17.707
They go, "Fuck them crackers."

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:19.603
Point blank.

00:09:19.603 --> 00:09:21.795
And I can see it now, you know,

00:09:21.795 --> 00:09:23.377
"Fuck them niggers over there."

00:09:23.377 --> 00:09:26.375
You know, it would just be there,

00:09:26.375 --> 00:09:29.792
I think because is never going anywhere.

00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:34.580
Back down in Louisiana
where I was originally born,

00:09:35.438 --> 00:09:39.372
Shreveport, Louisiana, it's
still down there today.

00:09:39.372 --> 00:09:42.930
Still down there today,
it ain't going nowhere.

00:09:45.990 --> 00:09:48.380
I've been trying to, I don't know,

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:50.540
I'm trying to change
a little bit by myself

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:52.150
I try to tell some of
the kids out there today,

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:55.382
you know, gang banging ain't what it was

00:09:55.382 --> 00:09:57.976
when I was gang banging.

00:09:57.976 --> 00:10:00.110
I couldn't just close my
eyes and just start shooting.

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:04.113
Kill a baby, a five year
old, something like that,

00:10:05.449 --> 00:10:06.949
because I have to.

00:10:13.470 --> 00:10:15.660
I'm kind of hanging in there you know?

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:17.803
It was nice to have
you listen to me today.

00:10:19.221 --> 00:10:20.080
- [Interviewer] Well thank you so much

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:21.050
for sharing your story.

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:21.883
- I appreciate that.

00:10:21.883 --> 00:10:23.020
- [Interviewer] I appreciate it.

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:23.853
Thank you.

